{
  "case_id": "2009-09-475",
  "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Biotech crops have produced enormous benefits for the nation's farmers and consumers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court in this case issued a broad-based injunction against the planting of a highly beneficial, genetically engineered alfalfa crop. In entering and sustaining that injunction, the courts below erred in two fundamental respects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stewart",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, we said in our brief in opposition that the fact that the EIS process was ongoing was a reason for this Court to deny certiorari. I think regardless of how good an argument that was at the cert stage, the Court has granted cert, and we think that the Court should decide the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: But our -- our core point here is that what we were proposing for the interim, that is allowing continued planting subject to various protective measures, was fundamentally different from the action on which the EIS was being prepared."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But as far as the court is concerned, it's conceded that NEPA was violated, an EIS was required. And then the district court vacates the deregulation decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do you -- do you agree that when you\u2019re talking about the elements of the injunction that are short of remand to the agency, that the Respondents do not have the obligation to meet the injunction standards with respect to those?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Do you agree -- would you agree that if the district court had just said the deregulating decision is vacated and Roundup Ready alfalfa is once again a regulated article, period, that would be okay? And you would have no basis to prevent this from going straight back to the agency?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would say that the mistake that was made was in not appreciating, though it was called to his attention by the lawyers I -- by the party I represent, that the vacatur did have this effect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus (rice growers)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the rice growers' brief makes clear -- the amicus brief makes clear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It will hasten the demise of organic farming, a rapidly developing business in this country --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: That is not alone a sufficient harm to justify an injunction, is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How do you answer\nMr. Robbins\u2019s --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: In terms of going back for the\nimminence, we\u2019re operating under this injunction which is\nunlawful. It's preventing -- it's causing real harm to\nthe nation's farmers today. There couldn't be more\nimminence in terms of the harm that we suffer because of\nthis erroneous injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are no instances in this record of any cross-pollination with hay, only a couple of -- a few isolated with respect to seed, and their harm really boils down to the question of their psychological objection to genetically engineered alfalfa. That harm is not cognizable under"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-09-475",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad593954159f4c645054c9f816055b126286c8819af862be25e8322338302ae4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad593954159f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel.\nThe case is submitted."
    },
